    chineseTitle: "阿里巴巴與四十大盜",
    passage: `Day 1\nAli Baba was a hardworking but poor woodcutter. One day, while he was gathering wood in the forest, he spotted a group of 40 thieves approaching in the distance. He quickly climbed a tree to hide and watch. The leader stepped up to a large rock and called out, "Open, sesame!" A door appeared in the rock, the men filed inside, and the door closed behind them.\n\nWhen the coast was clear, Ali Baba climbed down and tried the words himself. The door opened, and inside the cave, he found gold, jewels, and silk. He took only a modest amount and quietly made his way home.\n\nHis brother Cassim soon found out and insisted on going to the cave himself. Ali Baba warned him to be careful, but Cassim was too greedy to listen. He entered the cave without trouble—yet in his excitement, he completely forgot the magic words to get back out. When the thieves returned and saw him inside, they killed him as a warning to anyone else who might dare enter their secret spot.\n\nDay 2\nAli Baba recovered his brother's body, but this helped the thieves realize that someone else knew their secret. Their leader came up with a plan. He disguised himself as an oil seller and asked to stay the night at Ali Baba's home. He also hid his men, who were ready to attack on his signal, inside large oil jars.\n\nThat night, Morgiana, a clever slave girl, went to get some oil from the jars and found the hiding men. Before anyone could make a move, she poured boiling oil into each jar and killed them all. When their leader gave his signal and got no answer, he ran away in fear.\n\nHe came back once more and pretended to be a guest at a feast. However, Morgiana knew who he was. As she danced for the guests, she drew a hidden dagger and struck him down before he could do anything. To thank her for her courage and quick thinking, Ali Baba granted Morgiana her freedom. He shared the treasure wisely and spent the rest of his days in peace.`,
